From ed0acd63a3e64654ca4523079747de26b3efc988 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:20:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] XHCI X3: contexts, Address Device, EP0 control transfers

Per-slot/endpoint state joins the controller: for every enabled slot
the model keeps each endpoint's transfer-ring consumer (dequeue +
cycle), EP state, Max Packet Size and EP Type, all wiped by HCRST and
Disable Slot and carried by snapshots as part of the device state.

Address Device reads the guest's Input Context (ICC Add flags, Slot
and EP0 contexts in 32-byte CSZ=0 layout) and writes the Output Device
Context through DCBAA exactly where the guest looks: slot dword3 gets
Slot State Addressed (Default with BSR) and the hardware address
(= slot id), the EP0 output context reads Running with the live
dequeue pointer. Configure Endpoint installs Add-flagged contexts,
drops Drop-flagged ones, deconfigures on DC, and moves the slot to
Configured. Evaluate Context refreshes Max Packet Size and EP Type
only -- the guest's xhci_update_max_packet0 passes ring-base|producer
cycle in the dequeue field, so applying that field would rewind the
consumer; a vector moves the ring, evaluates, and proves the next TD
answers. Reset/Stop Endpoint and Set TR Dequeue Pointer maintain the
same internal state and mirror it into the output context. Refusals:
11 Slot Not Enabled (also for Configure/Evaluate before Address),
14 Endpoint Not Enabled, 5 TRB Error (bad ids / missing DCBAA entry).

Control transfers run on EP0 at the slot doorbell (value = target
endpoint, as the guest rings it): one Setup/[Data]/Status TD executes
against the same MSC device EP0 the UHCI/EHCI models serve
(0525:a4a5 descriptors, SET/GET_CONFIGURATION, GET_STATUS,
GET_MAX_LUN) and posts exactly one Transfer Event -- the guest's
wait takes the first slot+EP match and parks later events, so a
second event would poison the next transfer. Short IN reads complete
cc 13 Short Packet with residue = untransferred bytes in the event
Status dword[23:0] (the only residue the guest believes); exact reads
complete cc 1. A refused request completes cc 6 Stall Error and halts
the endpoint -- queued TDs do not move -- until the guest's recovery
(Reset Endpoint + Set TR Dequeue to its enqueue point) runs.

tests/test_xhci.c gains four groups (17 total) replaying the guest's
xhci_address_device and recovery code field for field: the slot-state
output gate, descriptor reads (8-byte MPS discovery, short 256->32
config read with residue, strings), the stall/halt/recover cycle, and
Configure/Evaluate incl. the dequeue-move trap. The X2 "unknown
command" vector now expects the refined cc 11 for Address Device on an
unenabled slot. NC: src/xhci.c reverted to X2 -> 39 failures. Gates:
make test, make test-sanitize, both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green.

Stated X3 boundary: transfers run on EP0 only (bulk/interrupt rings
are X4) and an addressed slot reaches the built-in device regardless
of port state (port presence is X5).
